const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"测量的是政策相关的不确定性",en:"The target is policy-related uncertainty"},body:{zh:"作者希望捕捉谁制定政策、何时采取何种政策以及其经济影响等不确定性，也包含长期财政问题。它不是把所有政治报道加总，更不是一般经济波动的同义词。论文正式版聚焦报纸文本，早期草稿中的其他成分不能不加区别地混入。",en:"The target includes uncertainty about policymakers, policy actions, timing and economic consequences, including long-horizon fiscal questions. It is not a count of all political reporting or a synonym for economic volatility. The final article focuses on newspapers; components from earlier drafts should not be silently mixed into that definition."},reference:{url:"https://users.ssc.wisc.edu/~mchinn/bakerbloomdavis_QJE2016.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2016年期刊版，第1598页",en:"Source: 2016 journal article, pp. 1598"}}},{title:{zh:"同一篇报道必须满足三类词",en:"An article must meet three term categories"},body:{zh:"美国月度指数在十家报纸中寻找同时包含不确定性、经济和政策三类词的文章，政策词包括国会、赤字、联储等及其变体。只出现政策关键词并不足够。跨语言扩展也需要重新设计词表与语境判断，不能把英文关键词逐字翻译就当作同一测量。",en:"The US monthly index searches ten newspapers for articles containing uncertainty, economy and policy terms together, including policy terms such as Congress, deficit and the Federal Reserve. A policy mention alone is insufficient. A new language requires reconsidering vocabulary and context rather than assuming literal translation preserves the measure."},reference:{url:"https://users.ssc.wisc.edu/~mchinn/bakerbloomdavis_QJE2016.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2016年期刊版，第1599页",en:"Source: 2016 journal article, pp. 1599"}}},{title:{zh:"先除以报道总量，再合成指数",en:"Normalize newspaper counts before combining them"},body:{zh:"原始命中数先除以同一报纸同月全部文章数，再将各报纸序列按1985至2009年标准差缩放，按月平均后把基期均值设为100。100是尺度约定，不是100%的概率。新闻总量增加本身不应自动被解读为政策不确定性同比例上升。",en:"Matches are divided by each newspaper's total monthly article count, scaled using its 1985–2009 standard deviation, averaged across papers and normalized to a baseline mean of 100. That 100 is a scale convention, not a probability. More news volume alone should not imply proportionately greater uncertainty."},reference:{url:"https://users.ssc.wisc.edu/~mchinn/bakerbloomdavis_QJE2016.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2016年期刊版，第1599页",en:"Source: 2016 journal article, pp. 1599"}}},{title:{zh:"日度版不是月度版的简单拆分",en:"The daily series uses a different archive"},body:{zh:"日度指数使用Newsbank更广泛的报纸集合，而不是把十家报纸的月度值拆到每天。报纸会进入或离开资料库，覆盖变化可能影响长期走势。因此频率转换之外，还要保留资料库构成与版本；两个指数相关性高也不表示定义完全相同。",en:"The daily index draws on a broader Newsbank archive rather than splitting the ten-paper monthly value into days. Papers enter and leave that archive, potentially affecting longer-run behavior. Archive composition and vintages matter alongside frequency conversion; high correlation does not make the two constructions identical."},reference:{url:"https://users.ssc.wisc.edu/~mchinn/bakerbloomdavis_QJE2016.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2016年期刊版，第1600页",en:"Source: 2016 journal article, pp. 1600"}}},{title:{zh:"跨国与长历史需要调整词表",en:"Country and historical coverage need different choices"},body:{zh:"长历史指数扩展了经济和政策相关词汇，以适应早期报纸用语；不同国家的报纸覆盖也并不一致。单报纸来源可能更嘈杂，媒体环境还会影响什么被报道。比较指数水平之前，应先检查当地来源、词表和基期，而不是只把曲线放在一起。",en:"Long-span indexes expand economic and policy vocabulary to reflect earlier usage, while country indexes differ in newspaper coverage. A single-paper source can be noisier, and media conditions affect what is reported. Check local sources, term sets and baselines before comparing index levels on a shared chart."},reference:{url:"https://users.ssc.wisc.edu/~mchinn/bakerbloomdavis_QJE2016.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2016年期刊版，第1605–1606页",en:"Source: 2016 journal article, pp. 1605–1606"}}},{title:{zh:"政治事件不一定形成指数峰值",en:"Political turbulence need not produce an EPU spike"},body:{zh:"论文指出一些政府停摆虽获大量报道，却很少同时出现经济与不确定性用语，因此未必带来明显峰值。这不是自动证明指数错误，而是提醒读者理解它的筛选目标。它衡量特定报道中的关注，不是给每次事件评定严重程度或因果影响。",en:"Some government shutdowns received extensive coverage without many articles simultaneously mentioning the economy and uncertainty. A missing spike is therefore not automatically a measurement failure. The index tracks a defined type of coverage, not the severity or causal economic impact of every political event."},reference:{url:"https://users.ssc.wisc.edu/~mchinn/bakerbloomdavis_QJE2016.pdf",label:{zh:"原文定位：2016年期刊版，第1598–1600页",en:"Source: 2016 journal article, pp. 1598–1600"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"EPU是新闻覆盖频率构成的代理指标，不是政策发生概率或市场涨跌预测。报纸构成、关键词与标准化区间不同，会影响跨国和跨时期比较。",en:"EPU is a newspaper-frequency proxy, not a policy-event probability or market-direction forecast. Newspaper coverage, keyword sets and normalization windows affect comparisons across countries and periods."}};export{e as default};
